WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.960
Judging from the e-mails I've been getting
from many of you, it sounds like much of my

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:13.499
audience agrees with me that it feels as though
American democracy is in peril.

00:00:13.499 --> 00:00:19.040
It's a sort of precarious state right now,
hanging on the brink with a president openly

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:24.990
saying the election is rigged, that the correct
result would be that he wins and that if he

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:31.289
doesn't win preemptively, he's saying it will
have been fraud and he will not necessarily

00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:33.010
leave the White House peacefully.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:34.530
So it's natural.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:35.530
It's common.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:40.370
It's logical to be feeling despair and helplessness.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:45.880
Right now, Donald Trump and his cronies have
gotten away with everything with so much.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:51.899
And our old friend John Nichols at The Nation
wrote a really great piece about the Bernie

00:00:51.899 --> 00:00:57.380
Sanders toolkit for defending against Donald
Trump's threats to democracy.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:03.110
Bernie Sanders actually spoke at George Washington
University last week and went through what

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:04.600
must happen.

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:10.470
And I think this is useful both to understand
the nuts and bolts, but also just to have

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.390
some hope, some hope.

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:13.670
So here are the ideas.

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:16.320
Bernie's plan to defend democracy.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:19.950
Number one, establish a nonpartisan commission
to oversee the election.

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:24.530
Now, the devil is always in the details with
these nonpartisan commissions.

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:31.080
But but that is the idea have by far the largest
voter turnout in American history.

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:34.530
Bernie and I, 110 percent aligned on this.

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:40.560
I've been saying for months now, whatever
the reality is going to be about voter suppression,

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:47.450
whatever else the biggest ever turnout is
the starting point to trying to remove Donald

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:48.450
Trump.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:51.560
People should vote as early as possible, says
Bernie.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:52.560
Absolutely.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:57.260
The earlier you vote either through in-person
early voting or vote by mail or hand delivering

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:00.590
your absentee ballot, the earlier the better.

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:05.760
All state legislatures must allow mail in
ballots to be counted before Election Day.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.090
This is key.

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:09.770
32 states already allow this.

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:10.789
Some don't.

00:02:10.789 --> 00:02:19.150
If we can get a jump on counting mail in ballots,
we reduce the threat of the scenario in which

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:24.800
Donald Trump is slightly ahead in some key
states on Election Day and use his lawyers

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:29.099
to stop or slow down the counting of as yet
uncounted absentee ballots.

00:02:29.099 --> 00:02:32.400
The more ballots that are counted early, the
better off we are.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.819
News media should clarify, says Bernie.

00:02:35.819 --> 00:02:37.819
There is no longer a single election day.

00:02:37.819 --> 00:02:43.819
It's important that media also explain to
people you can vote now in many states.

00:02:43.819 --> 00:02:45.879
Early voting has started in many states.

00:02:45.879 --> 00:02:51.000
Mail in voting has started in many states,
and that it is not just about November 3rd

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.060
anymore.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:57.370
Social media companies must stop disinformation
from being spread on their platforms.

00:02:57.370 --> 00:03:04.130
We have a blockbuster story from Channel four
in the UK about Donald Trump's targeted deterrents

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:05.760
of black voters in 2016.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:08.240
And a big piece of that is social media.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:14.030
And it is also on the social media companies
to stop disinformation.

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:19.709
And there should be both congressional in
DC and state hearings and state legislatures

00:03:19.709 --> 00:03:25.670
to explain how the election will be handled
in the event of all of these various scenarios.

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:29.030
Now, not all of these ideas are Bernie's original
ideas.

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:33.930
The nonpartizan commission, for example, was
the idea of former director of now national

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:35.720
intelligence, Dan Coats.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:39.379
The ACLU has been putting forth a lot of these
ideas, etc..

00:03:39.379 --> 00:03:44.690
But the point is, there are things to do now
not waiting until later.

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:45.690
If we wait.

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:46.690
We lose.

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:51.440
Biden needs an army of lawyers ready to go
now, not on November 4th.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:57.610
We learned last week that at least some lawyers,
the DNC and the Biden campaign have at the

00:03:57.610 --> 00:03:58.610
ready.

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:02.530
Those lawyers need to not just be ostensibly
ready.

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:05.970
The lawyers need to know now, not later.

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:10.470
What are the different strategies that Donald
Trump's lawyers might use to swing the election

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:11.470
to him?

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:12.680
The time is now, not later.

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:15.049
We're at a structural disadvantage here.

00:04:15.049 --> 00:04:20.779
If we are playing defense and they are playing
offense, they only need one strategy we haven't

00:04:20.779 --> 00:04:21.799
thought of.

00:04:21.799 --> 00:04:23.240
They might have six strategies.

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:25.800
If we defend against five, they've got number
six.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:30.330
So there is a difficulty implicit in playing
defense in this way.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:32.120
But the time is now to think about it.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:33.969
Not not later.

00:04:33.969 --> 00:04:35.569
So get your absentee ballot.

00:04:35.569 --> 00:04:38.629
If that's your plan, you can go to vote, dawg.

00:04:38.629 --> 00:04:41.099
Slash absentee hyphen ballot.

00:04:41.099 --> 00:04:44.259
Very important vote, dawg.

00:04:44.259 --> 00:04:47.460
Forward slash absentee hyphen.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:49.500
That's the dash ballot.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:51.669
You can also just Google vote, dawg.

00:04:51.669 --> 00:04:52.669
Absentee ballot.

00:04:52.669 --> 00:04:56.699
It'll be the first link that comes up and
we are linking to that Web site in the description

00:04:56.699 --> 00:04:57.830
to the YouTube video.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.229
I tracked my.

00:04:59.229 --> 00:05:04.819
Yesterday here in Massachusetts, it's currently
pending, it shows that my primary ballot was,

00:05:04.819 --> 00:05:05.819
of course, received.

00:05:05.819 --> 00:05:07.689
They voted absentee in the primary.

00:05:07.689 --> 00:05:09.249
They haven't been sent out yet.

00:05:09.249 --> 00:05:11.490
Most states have tracking systems.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:12.490
Vote, dawg.

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:16.559
Org tell you exactly how to register in any
state in which you live.

00:05:16.559 --> 00:05:18.669
Very, very important.

00:05:18.669 --> 00:05:19.970
Bernie has a plan.

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:21.310
We need plans.

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:22.379
We need strategy.

00:05:22.379 --> 00:05:27.659
We can't wait until 11 p.m. on November 3rd
when the Trump lawyers get ready to petition

00:05:27.659 --> 00:05:30.360
courts to stop the counting of absentee ballots.

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:32.520
We wait until then, we're done.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:36.539
So that's why it's so important to move on
this right now.

00:05:36.539 --> 00:05:42.639
And there we can all do something, even if
it's just having a plan that increases the

00:05:42.639 --> 00:05:45.169
likelihood of your vote being tallied correctly.

00:05:45.169 --> 00:05:46.169
That's a plan.

00:05:46.169 --> 00:05:47.169
That's something we can do.

00:05:47.169 --> 00:05:48.169
Yes, you can.

00:05:48.169 --> 00:05:49.169
Phone bank.

00:05:49.169 --> 00:05:51.599
Yes, you can volunteer to be a poll worker,
so on and so forth

